  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes the OptSHQCNN framework for phishing URL detection combining classical deep learning with a conceptual variational quantum circuit layer. Evaluated on four datasets (ISCX‑URL‑2016, URL‑based phishing, Mendeley‑2020, PhishStorm), it reports up to 99.72% accuracy, 99.76% precision, 99.32% recall, 99.54% F1, and 0.34% FPR, but the quantum component was not executed on a quantum simulator or hardware and was instead implemented using classical frameworks.",
